### 7.2 Database Layer Internal Architecture

`database.py` is the sole data-access layer. It abstracts both SQLite (local dev) and PostgreSQL (Render production) behind the same function signatures. The `_USE_PG` flag, set at module load time from `DATABASE_URL`, routes every `_execute()` call to the appropriate driver.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph database_py["backend/database.py"]
        direction TB
        CONN["_connect()\nReturns sqlite3 or psycopg2 connection\nbased on _USE_PG flag"]
        EXEC["_execute(conn, sql, params)\n_insert_id(conn, sql, params)\nUnified query helpers"]

        subgraph AuthFns["Auth & Session"]
            AF1["verify_credentials(email, password)"]
            AF2["create_session(user_id) → token"]
            AF3["get_session_user_id(token) → int"]
            AF4["change_password(user_id, ...) → bool"]
        end

        subgraph UserFns["User Management"]
            UF1["get_user_by_id(user_id) → dict"]
            UF2["get_all_users(exclude_id) → list"]
            UF3["update_current_user(updates, user_id) → dict"]
            UF4["create_user(name, email, password, ...) → dict"]
            UF5["delete_user(user_id)"]
        end

        subgraph ProfileFns["Profile Sections"]
            PF1["add_experience / update_experience / delete_experience"]
            PF2["add_education / update_education / delete_education"]
            PF3["add_skill / delete_skill"]
            PF4["add_project / add_volunteering / add_honor"]
        end

        subgraph FeedFns["Feed & Posts"]
            FF1["get_all_posts() → list"]
            FF2["create_post(author_id, content, ...) → dict"]
            FF3["toggle_post_like(post_id, user_id) → dict"]
            FF4["add_post_comment(post_id, author_id, text) → dict"]
            FF5["delete_post(post_id, user_id)"]
        end

        subgraph SocialFns["Social & Jobs"]
            SF1["connect_user / accept_connection / toggle_following"]
            SF2["get_incoming_connection_requests"]
            SF3["toggle_saved_job / apply_to_job"]
            SF4["get_all_jobs() / get_job_by_id() / get_company_by_id()"]
        end

        subgraph CommFns["Messaging & Notifications"]
            CF1["get_conversations_for_user(user_id)"]
            CF2["send_message(conv_id, sender_id, text)"]
            CF3["get_all_notifications()"]
            CF4["mark_notification_read / mark_all_notifications_read"]
        end

        subgraph EventFns["Events"]
            EF1["get_all_events_with_attendance(user_id)"]
