## 11. Mermaid Diagram Prompts (for external LLMs)

If you need to regenerate the diagrams in another tool (e.g., ChatGPT, Claude.ai, Mermaid Live Editor), use these prompts:

---

### Prompt A — Story #1 Sequence Diagram

> Generate a Mermaid `sequenceDiagram` with these exact participants and variable names:
> - `actor User as Student (User)`
> - `participant FE as Frontend (api.js)`
> - `participant BE as Flask app.py`
> - `participant OM as outreach.py`
> - `participant AI as AI Service (mocked P4 / Bedrock P5)`
> - `participant DB as data/ (in-memory)`
>
> Show this flow:
> 1. User → FE: "Clicks 'Get Message Help', selects recipient, tone, goal"
> 2. FE → BE: `POST /api/outreach/generate` with body `{ recipientId, tone, goal, custom_note }`
> 3. BE → DB: [get_user_by_id(recipientId)](file:///c:/Users/dhyan/OneDrive/Desktop/linkedin-redesign/backend/data/__init__.py#13-18)
> 4. DB → BE: recipient dict (or None)
> 5. `alt` block with three branches:
>    - `recipientId` missing → BE → FE: `400 { error: "recipientId is required" }`
>    - recipient not found → BE → FE: `404 { error: "User N not found" }`
>    - valid request → BE → OM: `generate_outreach_message(sender, recipient, context)` → OM → AI: `_call_ai(prompt)` → AI → OM: draft string → OM → BE: `{ draft, char_count, tone, tips, alternatives }` → BE → FE: 200 response → FE → User: display

---

### Prompt B — Story #7 Sequence Diagram

> Generate a Mermaid `sequenceDiagram` with these exact participants:
> - `actor User as Job Seeker (User)`
> - `participant FE as Frontend (api.js)`
> - `participant BE as Flask app.py`
> - `participant OM as outreach.py`
> - `participant DB as data/ (in-memory)`
>
> Show this flow:
> 1. User → FE: "Navigates to 'Message Someone'"
> 2. FE → BE: `GET /api/outreach/readiness`
> 3. BE → DB: resolve user (CURRENT_USER or userId param)
> 4. `alt` block:
>    - userId provided but not found → BE → FE: `404 { error: "User N not found" }`
>    - user resolved → BE → OM: `compute_outreach_readiness(user)` → OM internally runs "9 evaluator lambdas" → OM → BE: `{ score, max_score, level, breakdown, top_tips, can_message }` → BE → FE: 200 response
>    - nested `alt` on `can_message`: true → FE → User: "Show 'Ready to message!' badge"; false → FE → User: "Show warning + top_tips"

